\begin{abstract}
The AAAHSC--9.4 architecture introduces a sovereign-grade relativistic
simulation framework integrating secure multi-messenger telemetry,
GPU-resident adaptive mesh refinement (AMR), and BSSN $3+1$ spacetime
evolution into a unified computational instrument. The system achieves
Hamiltonian and momentum constraint norms at or below
$1.21 \times 10^{-13}$, enabling long-duration, multi-regime evolution
without secular drift or numerical decoherence. A lattice-based
post-quantum cryptographic encapsulation layer permits real-time
ingestion of Gaia DR3 astrometry and LIGO O4 gravitational strain data
while preserving data provenance and simulation integrity. GPU-native
boundary kernels perform prolongation, restriction, and flux
synchronization entirely on-device, eliminating CPU bottlenecks and
supporting exascale scalability. Semiclassical Hawking backreaction is
modeled through dynamically stabilized negative-energy sinks incorporated
directly into the stress-energy tensor. Combined with Kubernetes/MPI
multi-node orchestration, AAAHSC--9.4 establishes a new paradigm for
secure, high-fidelity relativistic simulation and represents a
significant advancement in computational physics, gravitational modeling,
and sovereign scientific computation.
\end{abstract}

